/**
 * Real GuestFs (lib/mods/guest-fs.ts) over ONE SSH connection to a game VM.
 *
 * Auth order matches lib/sftp.ts: the per-server management key first, then
 * the root password. (worker/game-mods.ts's older transport was password-only,
 * which is why a live Rust install failed "All configured authentication
 * methods failed" on a server whose password login had been turned off.)
 *
 * Reads/writes go over SFTP. The few things SFTP can't do portably (mkdir -p,
 * an overwriting move, recursive delete, chown) are fixed shell verbs whose
 * only arguments are paths that passed lib/mods/paths.ts `isSafeAbs` and are
 * single-quoted on top of that.
